From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:52:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/18] Round 7: Borrow candidate IDs and size parameter
 vectors exactly

Candidate IDs now deserialize as Cow<str> borrowed from the request
text unless the JSON string has escapes, and parameter arrays are
collected in a 64-value stack buffer and copied once into an exactly
sized vector instead of a doubling Vec. Longer arrays still parse and
are rejected by the existing batch check. A new test compares values,
bits and every error message with the plain derive of 0.2.0 and checks
duplicate detection across escaped IDs.

Workload: invalid (1,024 full records with 63 parameters each), 11
samples against round 6.
Before median: 1.465 ms. After median: 1.262 ms. Speedup: 1.16x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
